 ;; THIS HARNESS CANNOT SCORE THE BLOCK AXIS OF A FIXED BOX, and the case
 ;; is kept as a permanent, explained failure rather than chased or
 ;; deleted. Every case shares ONE long scrolling page, and a `fixed` box
 ;; is measured against the viewport, so the browser's answer for its `y`
 ;; relative to this case is `-(this case's distance from the viewport
 ;; top)` at whatever scroll position the previous case's paint-order pass
 ;; left behind: measured -47.84 here, 0 if the same case is placed first
 ;; on the page, and a different number again as soon as a case is added
 ;; above it. There is no engine behaviour that can agree with a number
 ;; that moves when an unrelated case is inserted, so this case's fixed
 ;; box is one permanently disagreeing box on the geometry axis (3/4), and
 ;; no further `fixed` case is added to the corpus for the same reason.
 ;;
 ;; What IS measurable about `fixed` was measured directly instead, on a
 ;; probe page shaped like this one, and is pinned by unit tests rather
 ;; than here: the INLINE axis, where there is no scrolling. Brave puts a
 ;; `left: 0` fixed box at x=0 inside a `margin-left: 120px` wrapper (not
 ;; 120), `left: 50%` at half the VIEWPORT (378 of 756, not half the
 ;; wrapper), and `right: 0` at 749 = 756 - 7. See
 ;; layout-absolute-children.
 ;;
 ;; The LINE-structure comparison is ill-defined here for a related
 ;; reason: the fixed box overlaps the content beside it, so "which line
 ;; is this word on" has no single right answer -- the browser's own word
 ;; rects for the fixed box and for the flow text occupy the same band.
 {:id :position/fixed-leaves-flow
  :group :position
  ;; Measured on its OWN page (see run.cljs's isolated-oracle): a fixed box
  ;; is positioned against the viewport, so on the shared corpus page its
  ;; case-relative y is only "how far down the page this case sits" -- a
  ;; number that changes when a case is inserted above it. On its own page
  ;; the case is at the viewport origin and the browser's answer means what
  ;; it says.
  :oracle/isolated true
  :html "<div><div style=\"position: fixed; left: 300px; top: 0\">fixed</div><div>a</div><div>b</div></div>"}

